    achievement "She founded Black Girls CODE, creating a major pathway for girls of color to enter programming, technology, and entrepreneurship."
    impact-fit "Bryant creates impact by building educational pathways, supportive communities, and technical confidence for girls historically excluded from computing."
    appearance "behind-the-click-2019" title="Behind the Click: Securing the Future for Black Women and Girls in Tech" event="SXSW" year="2019" format="featured-session" {
        summary """
            Bryant discusses Black Girls CODE as technical instruction and as a supportive learning community built around curiosity, imagination, and connection. She argues that technical advancement without a community behind it is incomplete.

            The session connects community management, warmth, and education-and-mentorship by focusing on the conditions in which another person can belong, persist, and grow.
